{
  "title": "Ossification of the Posterior Longitudinal Ligament",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/spine/2046/ossification-of-the-posterior-longitudinal-ligament",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Nov 8 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Ossification of the posterior longitudinal ligament (OPLL) is an idiopathic cervical spine anomaly that is a common cause of cervical myelopathy in the Asian population",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with lateral radiographs of the cervical spine. CT scan is the study of choice to determine the extent and thickness of the ossification",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation in patients with minimal symptoms. Surgical decompression followed by stabilization is indicated for patients with myelopathy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Asian (most common, but not limited to)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**men** are more commonly affected than women",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "most common levels are **C4-5 and C5-6**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "95% of ossification is located in the cervical spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "cause is unclear, but likely multifactorial",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "associated factors include:",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**diabetes**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "obesity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "high-salt, low-meat diet",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "poor calcium absorption",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "mechanical stress on the posterior longitudinal ligament",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "often asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "myelopathic symptoms",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "myelopathy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lateral radiograph often shows ossification of PLL",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/2046/images/xray%20lateral.jpg",
                  "caption": "Shows OPLL"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "used to evaluate the sagittal alignment of cervical spine",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "study of choice to evaluate spinal cord compression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "CT",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "study of choice to delineate the bony anatomy of the ossified posterior longitudinal ligament",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "observation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indicated only in patients with mild symptoms who are not candidates for surgery",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "direct or indirect surgical decompression, followed by stabilization",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "most patients with significant symptoms",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Techniques",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Interbody fusion without decompression**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "dynamic myelopathy",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "the theory behind this technique is that eliminating motion at stenotic levels prevents trauma to the cord",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Anterior corpectomy with or without OPLL resection**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "patients with a kyphotic cervical spine where posterior decompression is not an option",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "technique",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "one method to avoid a dural tear is to perform a corpectomy, and instead of removing the OPLL from the dura, allow it to \"**float**\" in the corpectomy site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Posterior laminoplasty or laminectomy with fusion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "indications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "only effective in patients with a **lordotic spine,** as it allows the spinal cord to drift away from the anterior compression from the OPLL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "considered a safer and preferable approach due to the difficulty of resecting the OPLL off the dura from an anterior approach",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "techniques",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "fusion should accompany laminectomy to avoid post-laminectomy kyphosis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "complications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "risk of postoperative OPLL growth",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence of OPLL**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "reduced with",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "complete resection",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "leaving OPLL to float into a corpectomy site",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
